{"abstract":"Multilingual phone recognition models can learn language-independent pronunciation patterns from large volumes of spoken data and recognize them across languages. This potential can be harnessed to improve speech technologies for underresourced languages. However, these models are typically trained on phonological representations of speech sounds, which do not necessarily reflect the phonetic realization of speech. A mismatch between a phonological symbol and its phonetic realizations can lead to phone confusions and reduce performance. This work introduces formant-based vowel categorization aimed at improving cross-lingual vowel recognition by uncovering a vowel's phonetic quality from its formant frequencies, and reorganizing the vowel categories in a multilingual speech corpus to increase their consistency across languages. The work investigates vowel categories obtained from a trilingual multi-dialect speech corpus of Danish, Norwegian, and Swedish using three categorization techniques. Cross-lingual phone recognition experiments reveal that uniting vowel categories of different languages into a set of shared formant-based categories improves cross-lingual recognition of the shared vowels, but also interferes with recognition of vowels not present in one or more training languages. Cross-lingual evaluation on regional dialects provides inconclusive results. Nevertheless, improved recognition of individual vowels can translate to improvements in overall phone recognition on languages unseen during training.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stepanovic, Marija","Hardmeier, Christian","Scharenborg, Odette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828139"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"keyword":["Consonants","Phonetics","Phonology","Speech communication","Speech production","Speech sounds","Vocalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formant based vowel categorization for cross lingual phone recognition","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0036222","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828139","identifier":[{"id":"105001235132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-12ef8a63-313d-4de7-aa6b-9d7bdf775946"],"keyword":["Consonants","Covariance and correlation","Human voice","Phonetics","Phonology","Speech communication","Speech production","Speech sounds","Vocalization","Vowel systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-73E5C15772ED7F663171FEB8C895B34D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1121/10.0036222","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Odette","key":"scharenborgpau","last":"Scharenborg","name":"Scharenborg, Odette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-12ef8a63-313d-4de7-aa6b-9d7bdf775946"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formant-Based Vowel Categorization for Cross-Lingual Phone Recognition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828139","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Multilingual automatic phone recognition models can learn language independent pronunciation patterns from large volumes of spoken data and recognize them across languages. This potential can be harnessed to improve speech technologies for under-resourced languages. However, these models are typically trained on phonological representations of speech sounds, which do not necessarily reflect the phonetic realization of speech. A mismatch between a phonological symbol and its phonetic realizations can lead to phone confusions and reduce performance. This thesis introduces a formant-based vowel categorization method aimed at improving cross-lingual vowel recognition by uncovering a vowel’s phonetic quality from its formant frequencies, and reorganizing the vowel categories in a multilingual speech corpus to increase their consistency across languages. The work investigates vowel categories obtained from a trilingual speech corpus of Danish, Norwegian, and Swedish using four categorization techniques. Crosslingual phone recognition experiments reveal that uniting the vowel categories of different languages into a shared set of formant-based categories can improve cross-lingual recognition of the shared vowels, but also interfere with recognition of vowels not present in one or more training languages. Nevertheless, improved recognition of individual vowels can translate to improvements in overall phone recognition on languages unseen during training. To assess their wider applicability in automatic speech recognition (ASR), the investigated vowel representations are also evaluated as part of pronunciation lexicons used in hybrid ASR systems. These experiments, however, do not reveal many conclusive patterns, which demonstrates that hybrid systems are more robust to divergence in pronunciation from the phonological norm. Nonetheless, a qualitative analysis of phone predictions shows that the models trained on formant-based vowel representations can infer the distinctive vowel qualities of an unseen language, especially when their vowel set and training data align with the vowel system of the target language. This indicates that formant-based vowel representations could provide useful information for tasks where phonological description is preferred.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Stepanovic, Marija"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798543"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phonetic vowel representations for cross lingual automatic speech recognition","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://en.itu.dk/-/media/EN/Research/PhD-Programme/PhD-defences/2024/Marija-thesis-pdf.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798543","ids":["itu-8255d8a3-64d3-4d19-8163-2713e86466a0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8544935599DA99EEBFB419073EDDD344"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"232","pages":"244","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8255d8a3-64d3-4d19-8163-2713e86466a0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Phonetic Vowel Representations for Cross-Lingual Automatic Speech Recognition","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798543","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The lack of publicly available evaluation data for low-resource languages limits progress in Spoken Language Understanding (SLU). As key tasks like intent classification and slot filling require abundant training data, it is desirable to reuse existing data in high-resource languages to develop models for low-resource scenarios. We introduce XSID, a new benchmark for cross-lingual (X) Slot and Intent Detection in 13 languages from 6 language families, including a very low-resource dialect. To tackle the challenge, we propose a joint learning approach, with English SLU training data and non-English auxiliary tasks from raw text, syntax and translation for transfer. We study two setups which differ by type and language coverage of the pre-trained embeddings. Our results show that jointly learning the main tasks with masked language modeling is effective for slots, while machine translation works best for intent classification.","author_count":9,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob","Sharaf, Ibrahim","Imankulova, Aizhan","Üstün, Ahmet","Stepanovic, Marija","Ramponi, Alan","Khairunnisa, Siti Oryza","Komachi, Mamoru","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384367"],"event":{"acronym":"NAACL HLT","title":"Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Japan","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Factmata","Tokyo Metropolitan University","University of Groningen","University of Trento"],"keyword":["Cross lingual benchmarks","Intent classification","Low resource languages","Slot filling","Spoken Language Understanding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from masked language modeling to translation non english auxiliary tasks improve zero shot spoken language understanding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85927075/1050_Paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384367","ids":["itu-d2d5d052-9bdc-4831-838b-2b7215d6dc52"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual benchmarks","Intent classification","Low-resource languages","Slot filling","Spoken Language Understanding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BFA7465C4DF53E4F45C222B730B76467"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85927075/1050_Paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85979953/2021.naacl_main.197.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"factmata","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Factmata","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"tokyo metropolitan university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo Metropolitan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university of trento","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Trento","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ibrahim","key":"sharafpau","last":"Sharaf","name":"Sharaf, Ibrahim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Aizhan","key":"imankulovapau","last":"Imankulova","name":"Imankulova, Aizhan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmet","key":"üstünpau","last":"Üstün","name":"Üstün, Ahmet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"ramponipau","last":"Ramponi","name":"Ramponi, Alan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Siti Oryza","key":"khairunnisapau","last":"Khairunnisa","name":"Khairunnisa, Siti Oryza","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mamoru","key":"komachipau","last":"Komachi","name":"Komachi, Mamoru","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of NAACL"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d2d5d052-9bdc-4831-838b-2b7215d6dc52"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Masked Language Modeling to Translation: Non-English Auxiliary Tasks Improve Zero-shot Spoken Language Understanding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384367","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Digital assistants are becoming an integral part of everyday life. However, commercial digital assistants are only available for a limited set of languages. Because of this, a vast amount of people can not use these devices in their native tongue. In this work, we focus on two core tasks within the digital assistant pipeline: intent classification and slot detection. Intent classification recovers the goal of the utterance, whereas slot detection identifies important properties regarding this goal. Besides introducing a novel cross-lingual dataset for these tasks, consisting of 11 languages, we evaluate a variety of models: 1) multilingually pretrained transformer-based models, 2) we supplement these models with auxiliary tasks to evaluate whether multi-task learning can be beneficial, and 3) annotation transfer with neural machine translation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob","Stepanovic, Marija","Ramponi, Alan","Sharaf, Ibrahim","Üstün, Ahmet","Imankulova, Aizhan","Khairunnisa, Siti Oryza","Komachi, Mamoru","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384654"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Japan","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Factmata","Tokyo Metropolitan University","University of Groningen"],"keyword":["Cross lingual dataset","Digital assistants","Intent classification","Multilingual transformers","Slot detection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cross lingual multi task transfer for zero shot task oriented dialog","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://robvanderg.github.io/doc/resourceful2020.1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384654","ids":["itu-e5ccae92-4344-4d08-a3e7-75fbd93d60bb"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual dataset","Digital assistants","Intent classification","Multilingual transformers","Slot detection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-035EB0905B4DC804F3599318935E2B62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://robvanderg.github.io/doc/resourceful2020.1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"factmata","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Factmata","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"jp","key":"tokyo metropolitan university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo Metropolitan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"ramponipau","last":"Ramponi","name":"Ramponi, Alan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ibrahim","key":"sharafpau","last":"Sharaf","name":"Sharaf, Ibrahim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmet","key":"üstünpau","last":"Üstün","name":"Üstün, Ahmet","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Aizhan","key":"imankulovapau","last":"Imankulova","name":"Imankulova, Aizhan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Siti Oryza","key":"khairunnisapau","last":"Khairunnisa","name":"Khairunnisa, Siti Oryza","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mamoru","key":"komachipau","last":"Komachi","name":"Komachi, Mamoru","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e5ccae92-4344-4d08-a3e7-75fbd93d60bb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cross-lingual Multi-task Transfer for Zero-shot Task-oriented Dialog","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384654","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces FT Speech, a new speech corpus created from the recorded meetings of the Danish Parliament, otherwise known as the Folketing (FT). The corpus contains over 1,800 hours of transcribed speech by a total of 434 speakers. It is significantly larger in duration, vocabulary, and amount of spontaneous speech than the existing public speech corpora for Danish, which are largely limited to read-aloud and dictation data. We outline design considerations, including the preprocessing methods and the alignment procedure. To evaluate the quality of the corpus, we train automatic speech recognition systems on the new resource and compare them to the systems trained on the Danish part of Språkbanken, the largest public ASR corpus for Danish to date. Our baseline results show that we achieve a 14.01 WER on the new corpus. A combination of FT Speech with in-domain language data provides comparable results to models trained specifically on Språkbanken, showing that FT Speech transfers well to this data set. Interestingly, our results demonstrate that the opposite is not the case. This shows that FT Speech provides a valuable resource for promoting research on Danish ASR with more spontaneous speech.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","Stepanovic, Marija","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382592"],"event":{"acronym":"INTERSPEECH","title":"Annual Conference of the International Speech Communication Association"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danish language","Speech corpus","Speech recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ft speech danish parliament speech corpus","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85251455/FT_Speech_INTERSPEECH2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382592","identifier":[{"id":"85098229116","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-592b099d-7681-4c81-bfc5-7b9ce5ac7d7b"],"keyword":["Danish language","speech corpus","speech recognition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-315EED0D3334E548C55175F4DE22DB8A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85251455/FT_Speech_INTERSPEECH2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Søeborg","key":"kirkedalpau","last":"Kirkedal","name":"Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marija","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Marija","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21437/interspeech.2020-3164","publisher":"International Speech Communication Association (ISCA)","series":"Annual Conference of the International Speech Communication Association","status":"p","title":"INTERSPEECH 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098229116"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-592b099d-7681-4c81-bfc5-7b9ce5ac7d7b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FT Speech: Danish Parliament Speech Corpus","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382592","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
